{
 "_": "The Phobos material sets, revision 3. tiles: a named tile is a source (src, or the best-seamed of src_any) from tools/phobos/textures/catalog.json, laid m metres across, 'course' (plain repeat: coursed stone, brick, planks, big-stone rubble) or 'random' (the shader may scatter repeats), of a class (cls: stone, brick, plaster, wood, cloth, wet, metal; sets roughness and relief), with pale or dark mortar, graded by a named grade. joints: [r, g, b, amount] paints the tile's joints, cracks and grooves that colour after grading (the Keep's bone-pale joints, ash in charred grooves). grades: value = mean brightness 0..1 of the sRGB picture after grading, sat = saturation kept, tint = colour multiply, contrast = how much of the picture's own light and dark is kept. sets: which tile plays which part where. Districts are told apart by hue and stone size, not brightness; nothing is under 0.10 or over 0.36. Built by tools/phobos/textures/build_sets.py into assets/game/phobos/tex/. No blue with gold, no letters, no heraldry. placeholder: a stand-in to be used on nothing larger than a prop until a real one is painted (iron, rust iron, the Ossuary's wall).",
